== ARCHIVE: Step M rerun with the shipped script, after the freeze-plan refactor ==

This is the second run of the same ladder, and it exists for one reason: the archived
`20260930T212300Z_stepm_ladder.out` was produced by `step_m_ccsdt.py` *before* the
frozen-core selection was refactored into a single `freeze_plan()` entry point. A paper
may not cite numbers whose producing code no longer exists, so the ladder was re-run with
what the package now ships.

Reproduction, checked field by field rather than asserted: both files were reduced to
their basis headers, rung markers, MP2/CCSD/CCSD(T) rows and RHF lines, with every
trailing wall-clock column stripped. 60 such lines each; five differ, and all five are the
one print statement whose wording changed ("冻核数 1/1（复合物 2）" became
"每片段冻核 [1, 1]，合计 2"). Not one energy, not one interaction-energy figure, not one
convergence flag differs. The refactor moved no number.

Why the earlier archive stays in this directory: the comparison above is only checkable if
both files exist. See README.md here for which one the paper cites.

Run: OMP_NUM_THREADS=16 MAXMEM_MB=12000 BASES="6-31g*,cc-pvdz,aug-cc-pvdz,cc-pvtz,aug-cc-pvtz"
     PYTHONPATH=. python3 -u nlcsplit/step_m_ccsdt.py   (PySCF 2.12.1, Python 3.10.12, WSL, EXIT=0)

Conventions are the ones stated in the first archive's header, unchanged: official S22 entry 2
(initial, unrelaxed geometry, O...O = 2.9104 A), counterpoise only, RHF reference,
MP2/CCSD/CCSD(T) from PySCF's own modules, frozen-O-1s and all-electron as two separate rungs
with the frozen count taken from the same call on both sides of the difference.

